      "title": "Show HN: Backplane \u2013 An AI Development Environment for Hardware",
      "summary": "We made Backplane to actually use Fable, Astra, etc. as real electrical engineers! It incorporates KiCad + your favorite harness (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Grok) to accelerate hardware development. You can use it \"autonomously\" or work alongside the agent, making changes or comments to redirect the agent as it works. Also has some slick skills for schematic editing, BOM management. Hardware is in its \"tab to accept changes\"/copilot era rather than its agentic era imo.",
      "summary_html": "<p>We made Backplane to actually use Fable, Astra, etc. as real electrical engineers! It incorporates KiCad + your favorite harness (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Grok) to accelerate hardware development. You can use it \"autonomously\" or work alongside the agent, making changes or comments to redirect the agent as it works. Also has some slick skills for schematic editing, BOM management.<p>Hardware is in its \"tab to accept changes\"/copilot era rather than its agentic era imo.</p>\n\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528196\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528196</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 1</p></p>",
